  "question": {
    "text": "Determine how many of the following statements are true at very high pressure for a real gas:<br />\r<br />\r<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Compressibility factor is greater than <math> <mrow> <mtext>1</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow> </math><br />\r<br />\r<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Compressibility factor varies linearly with pressure.<br />\r<br />\r<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Molar volume occupied by gas is more as compared to ideal gas at similar pressure and temperature.<br />\r<br />\r<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Gas is less compressible as compare to ideal gas.<br />\r<br />\r<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> Compressibility factor is given by <math> <mrow> <mtext>Z</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>=</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>1</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>+</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>Pb</mtext></mrow> <mrow> <mtext>RT</mtext></mrow> </mfrac> <mtext>.</mtext></mrow> </math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "At high pressure <math> <mrow>  <mtext>Z</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>&#x003E;</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>1</mtext></mrow></math>i.e. repulsive forces are relatively dominant, so gas is less compressible.<br>at high pressure, <math> <mrow>  <mtext>a</mtext><mo>&#x2245;</mo><mtext>0</mtext><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></math>",
